{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rb4azzT8hcEYLGYvcdrTi7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Taiwan news November 10 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Taiwan News\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_News\"},{\"title\":\"Front Page - Taipei Times\",\"url\":\"https://www.taipeitimes.com/News/front\"},{\"title\":\"Taiwan News - Voice of the People, Bridge to the World\",\"url\":\"https://www.taiwannews.com.tw/\"},{\"title\":\"Taiwan Journal\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_Journal\"},{\"title\":\"TVBS News\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TVBS_News\"},{\"title\":\"Taiwan Daily\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_Daily\"},{\"title\":\"TaiwanPlus\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TaiwanPlus\"},{\"title\":\"Taiwan News\",\"url\":\"https://www.newsnow.co.uk/h/World+News/Asia/Taiwan\"},{\"title\":\"Focus Taiwan - CNA English News\",\"url\":\"https://focustaiwan.tw/\"}]\n\nThe search didn't return anything dated specifically to November 10, 2026, so these are the most recent items I found, with dates where they were given.\n\n- **Focus Taiwan (CNA), listed as current:** Headlines include a Taiwan Railway change to its online ticket booking cutoff, a second batch of F-16V jets arriving, a live-fire drill in Kinmen, and President Lai's push for independent satellite launches. Taiwan wins 48 golds at Asian Sport Stacking Championships is also listed.\n- **Taiwan News, listed as 2 days old:** Coverage includes a magnitude 4.2 earthquake jolting central Taiwan, a rule change that bars Chinese-owned yachts, and a report on China's 'anaconda' strategy targeting Taiwan's outlying islands.\n- **Taipei Times front page:** On November 9, 2026, an investigation launched by Nvidia into its founder and CEO Jensen Huang over his affair with an alleged Chinese spy is unlikely to have a major impact on Taiwan's AI supply chain, according to a think-tank head. On November 6, Taiwan ordered the financial regulator to \"stabilize\" the stock market after a sell-off, and shares in TSMC plummeted as much as 9.8 percent. Also on November 6, prosecutors indicted independent Legislator May Chin and three aides on suspicion of receiving Chinese funding.\n\nTaken together, the most recent coverage points to a stock-market sell-off in early November, a Chinese-linked prosecution, and routine defense and local news. For a verified November 10 picture, the Focus Taiwan and Taipei Times front pages are the best places to check directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9381cf6c-cdc6-44c7-b9ca-614cb33d4c1a","uuid":"682a4566-8d64-454c-a6ec-9915ac4bddb9","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:56:19.905Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Taiwan news November 10 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01UGCJVewgFMT6LVFZbX3KPR","content":[{"title":"Taiwan News","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_News"},{"title":"Front Page - Taipei Times","url":"https://www.taipeitimes.com/News/front"},{"title":"Taiwan News - Voice of the People, Bridge to the World","url":"https://www.taiwannews.com.tw/"},{"title":"Taiwan Journal","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_Journal"},{"title":"TVBS News","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TVBS_News"},{"title":"Taiwan Daily","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan_Daily"},{"title":"TaiwanPlus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TaiwanPlus"},{"title":"Taiwan News","url":"https://www.newsnow.co.uk/h/World+News/Asia/Taiwan"},{"title":"Focus Taiwan - CNA English News","url":"https://focustaiwan.tw/"}]},"The search didn't return anything dated specifically to November 10, 2026, so these are the most recent items I found, with dates where they were given.\n\n- **Focus Taiwan (CNA), listed as current:** Headlines include a Taiwan Railway change to its online ticket booking cutoff, a second batch of F-16V jets arriving, a live-fire drill in Kinmen, and President Lai's push for independent satellite launches. Taiwan wins 48 golds at Asian Sport Stacking Championships is also listed.\n- **Taiwan News, listed as 2 days old:** Coverage includes a magnitude 4.2 earthquake jolting central Taiwan, a rule change that bars Chinese-owned yachts, and a report on China's 'anaconda' strategy targeting Taiwan's outlying islands.\n- **Taipei Times front page:** On November 9, 2026, an investigation launched by Nvidia into its founder and CEO Jensen Huang over his affair with an alleged Chinese spy is unlikely to have a major impact on Taiwan's AI supply chain, according to a think-tank head. On November 6, Taiwan ordered the financial regulator to \"stabilize\" the stock market after a sell-off, and shares in TSMC plummeted as much as 9.8 percent. Also on November 6, prosecutors indicted independent Legislator May Chin and three aides on suspicion of receiving Chinese funding.\n\nTaken together, the most recent coverage points to a stock-market sell-off in early November, a Chinese-linked prosecution, and routine defense and local news. For a verified November 10 picture, the Focus Taiwan and Taipei Times front pages are the best places to check directly."],"durationSeconds":7.385849736999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Rb4azzT8hcEYLGYvcdrTi7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
